        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glycosylglucose disaccharide, found most notably in milk, that consists of &lt;small&gt;D&lt;/small&gt;-galactose and &lt;small&gt;D&lt;/small&gt;-glucose fragments bonded through a β-1→4 glycosidic linkage. The glucose fragment can be in either the α- or β-pyranose form, whereas the galactose fragment can only have the β-pyranose form.</obo:IAO_0000115>
