        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35341"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hydroxycalciol that is calcidiol in which the &lt;em&gt;pro&lt;/em&gt;-&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt; hydrogen of calcidiol is replaced by a hydroxy group. It is the active form of vitamin D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt;, produced fom calciol &lt;em&gt;via&lt;/em&gt; hydoxylation in the liver to form calcidiol, which is subsequently oxidised in the kidney to give calcitriol.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>CHEBI:13932</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>CHEBI:19209</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
