    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_18258">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33709"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33853"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An iodothyronine compound having iodo substituents at the 3-, 3&apos;- and 5-positions. Although some is produced in the thyroid, most of the 3,3&apos;,5-triiodo-&lt;small&gt;L&lt;/small&gt;-thyronine in the body is generated by mono-deiodination of &lt;small&gt;L&lt;/small&gt;-thyroxine in the peripheral tissues. Its metabolic activity is about 3 to 5 times that of &lt;small&gt;L&lt;/small&gt;-thyroxine. The sodium salt is used in the treatment of hypothyroidism.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>CHEBI:11701</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
