        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33838"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pyrimidine nucleoside in which cytosine is attached to &lt;small&gt;D&lt;/small&gt;-arabinofuranose via a β-&lt;em&gt;N&lt;/em&gt;&lt;small&gt;&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;-glycosidic bond. Used mainly in the treatment of leukaemia, especially acute non-lymphoblastic leukaemia, cytarabine is an antimetabolite antineoplastic agent that inhibits the synthesis of DNA. It also has antiviral and immunosuppressant properties.</obo:IAO_0000115>
