        <obo:IAO_0000115>A naphthoate ester obtained by formal condensation of the carboxy group of 2-hydroxy-7-methoxy-5-methyl-1-naphthoic acid with the 5-hydroxy group of (1a&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;,5&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;,6&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;,6a&lt;i&gt;E&lt;/i&gt;,9a&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-5-hydroxy-1a-[(4&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-2-oxo-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl]-2,3,8,9-tetradehydro-1a,5,6,9a-tetrahydrocyclopenta[5,6]cyclonona[1,2-&lt;em&gt;b&lt;/em&gt;]oxiren-6-yl 2,6-dideoxy-2-(methylamino)-α-&lt;small&gt;D&lt;/small&gt;-galactopyranoside. The chromophoric part of neocarzinostatin, it is tightly and non-covelently bound to a 113-membered apoprotein, which serves to protect it and release it to the target DNA.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>CHEBI:41563</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
