        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24532"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A 2,6-diaminopurine that is (1&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;)-cyclopent-2-en-1-ylmethanol in which the &lt;em&gt;pro&lt;/em&gt;-&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt; hydrogen at the 4-position is substituted by a 2-amino-6-(cyclopropylamino)-9&lt;em&gt;H&lt;/em&gt;-purin-9-yl group. A nucleoside analogue reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) with antiretroviral activity against HIV, it is used (particularly as the sulfate) with other antiretrovirals in combination therapy of HIV infection.</obo:IAO_0000115>
