    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63599">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24532"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_26020"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A purine arabinonucleoside monophosphate having 2-fluoroadenine as the nucleobase. A prodrug, it is rapidly dephosphorylated to 2-fluoro-ara-A and then phosphorylated intracellularly by deoxycytidine kinase to the active triphosphate, 2-fluoro-ara-ATP. Once incorporated into DNA, 2-fluoro-ara-ATP functions as a DNA chain terminator. It is used for the treatment of adult patients with B-cell chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) who have not responded to, or whose disease has progressed during, treatment with at least one standard alkylating-agent containing regimenas.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>CHEBI:31616</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
