        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33575"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prostaglandin F&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;α&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; that is an analogue of prostaglandin F&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2α&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; in which the pentyl group has been replaced by 2-phenylethyl and where the the 13,14-double bond has undergone formal hydrogenation. Its isopropyl ester prodrug, latanoprost, is used in the treatment of open-angle glaucoma and ocular hypertension.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>cas:41639-83-2</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
