        <obo:IAO_0000115>A very long-chain fatty acid that is docosa-10,16-dienoic acid which is substituted by methyl groups at positions 4, 6, 8, 12, 14, 18 and 20, by hydroxy groups at positions 11, 19 and 21, and by a (2&apos;,5-dimethyloctahydro-2,2&apos;-bifuran-5-yl)ethanol group at position 21. An ionophore produced by &lt;em&gt;Streptomyces conglobatus&lt;/em&gt;, it is used in research to raise the intracellular level of Ca&lt;small&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; and as a research tool to understand Ca&lt;small&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; transport across biological membranes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>cas:56092-81-0</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
