        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_37622"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A member of the class of benzamides resulting from the formal condensation of the carboxy group of 4-amino-5-(ethylsulfonyl)-2-methoxybenzoic acid with the primary amino group of 2-(aminomethyl)-1-ethylpyrrolidine. It is a potent, selective dopamine D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; and D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; receptor antagonist. It is an atypical antipsychotic/antischizophrenic agent with limited extrapyrimidal side effects.</obo:IAO_0000115>
