        <obo:IAO_0000115>A naphthalenecarboxamide resulting from the formal condensation of the carboxylic acid group of 4-cyano-1-methoxynaphthalene-2-carboxylic acid with the primary amino group of 1-(1-butylpyrrolidin-2-yl]methanamine. It is a highly potent, competitive, preferential dopamine D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; receptor antagonist, centrally active upon systemic administration.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>cas:149649-22-9</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>lincs.smallmolecule:LSM-1755</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
