        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33575"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A monocarboxylic acid that is acetic acid in which one of the methyl hydrogens is replaced by bromine while a second is replaced by chlorine. A low-melting (27.5-31.5°C), hygroscopic crystalline solid, it can be formed during the disinfection (by chlorination) of water that contains bromide ions and organic matter, so can occur in drinking water as a byproduct of the disinfection process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>cas:5589-96-8</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>kegg.compound:C19212</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
