        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24532"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An azaspiro compound that consists of 1,3,8-triazaspiro[4.5]decan-4-one having a phenyl group attached to N-1 and a 3-(4-fluorophenoxy)propyl attached to N-8. Selective 5-HT antagonist, which binds to 5-HT&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; sites as potently as spiperone but has lower affinity for 5-HT&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2C&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; receptors. Also a high affinity D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; receptor antagonist (Ki = 3 nM). Lacks the disruptive effect of spiperone on animal behaviour.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>cas:510-74-7</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>lincs.smallmolecule:LSM-4124</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
