        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A methanesulfonate salt obtained from pergolide by mixing eqimolar amount of pergolide and methanesulfonic acid. A dopamine D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; receptor agonist which also has D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; and D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; agonist properties, it is used in the management of Parkinson&apos;s disease, although it was withdrawn from the U.S. and Canadian markets in 2007 due to an increased risk of cardiac valve dysfunction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>cas:66104-23-2</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
