        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_25705"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An organochlorine compound resulting from the epoxidation of the double bond of isodrin. It is the &lt;em&gt;endo&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;endo&lt;/em&gt; stereoisomer of dieldrin. It is an insecticide mainly used on field crops such as cotton and grains and has also been used as a rodenticide to control mice and voles. The product is banned in many countries since it is a persistent organic pollutant.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>agr:IND606456156</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
